# Visual Basic program

With `kind: Program` a Visual Basic script is a whole module: a `Sub Main` and any functions,
classes and structures it needs. Invoklet compiles it as written and starts `Main`.

```vb run
Module Program
    Sub Main()
        Dim inventory As New Inventory()
        inventory.Add("Keyboard", 3)
        inventory.Add("Mouse", 5)
        inventory.Add("Keyboard", 2)

        inventory.Lines().Dump("Inventory")
        Console.WriteLine($"Total items: {Total(inventory)}")
    End Sub

    Function Total(inventory As Inventory) As Integer
        Return inventory.Lines().Sum(Function(line) line.Quantity)
    End Function
End Module

Class Inventory
    Private ReadOnly _counts As New Dictionary(Of String, Integer)

    Public Sub Add(name As String, quantity As Integer)
        Dim current As Integer
        _counts.TryGetValue(name, current)
        _counts(name) = current + quantity
    End Sub

    Public Function Lines() As IEnumerable(Of StockLine)
        Return _counts.OrderBy(Function(pair) pair.Key).Select(Function(pair) New StockLine(pair.Key, pair.Value))
    End Function
End Class

Class StockLine
    Public Sub New(name As String, quantity As Integer)
        Me.Name = name
        Me.Quantity = quantity
    End Sub

    Public ReadOnly Property Name As String
    Public ReadOnly Property Quantity As Integer
End Class
```
